**Convention 7.2 (remaining mathematical and operational boundaries).**
The existence question for this code on this full fiber, and its first
possible two-call state budget, are settled by Theorems 4.1--6.1.
There is no classification here of all nine-state-compatible codes,
the general prescribed-code frontier, or an effective decision test
for an arbitrary supplied computable code. Other call budgets are not
classified; in particular no root-only impossibility for larger call
budgets follows from the two-call argument.

The conclusions require every service and access condition in Assumption
3.1 and the exact finite state-only restriction in Definition 3.2.
They construct no physical acquisition, export, isolation or entry
mechanism. An image inverse constructing a finite witness is not a
physical inverse operation on the register. No equivalence with physical
storage, time, energy, address cost or total work is asserted. A program
with a computed address, extra workspace or another source port requires
a separate correspondence before these state bounds apply. Nothing here
asserts an empirical machine-learning conclusion, external mathematical
priority, or a Lean/kernel-verification consequence.

